  "Bitcoin/Transaction.TaprootHasher.signatureHash": {
    "notes": "Closest published bitcoin 0.2.1 createTaprootKeySpendSignatureHash one-shot operation versus the plugin prepared hasher first cold signatureHash call. Both compute input 0 SIGHASH_DEFAULT on the identical ten-input/two-output transaction, with equal 34-byte spent scripts and no annex. Package transaction/script parsing and native prepareTaproot occur outside timing. Native lazy common hashes are cold and included; the pure package recomputes its common hashes per call and exposes no retained cache. Any ratio describes uncached package operation versus prepared-cold plugin operation, not equivalent reusable-hasher APIs. Native returns a Nat8 array; its conversion to Blob for the oracle is outside timing, while the plugin returns Blob directly."
  }
